{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ML3J8btWbPwuZizVimo3Fz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation of their ACR-VLA conformal refinement research project. Let me analyze the project context carefully.\n\nKey facts from the context:\n\n1. **MVP results (done)**: Per-DOF (B) consistently beats scalar (A) which beats no-conditioning (C) in a synthetic 3D point-reaching task. The advantage holds with K=10 samples (with Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage), though with some degradation (~15pp).\n\n2. **Core claims**:\n   - Claim 1: Per-DOF conformal features enable dimension-selective correction (kill criterion: A3 ablation gap < 2%)\n   - Claim 2: ACI+COC maintains calibrated uncertainty without external supervision (kill criterion: Spearman ρ < 0.3 AND no >10% ellipsoid volume narrowing)\n   - Claim 3: ACR-VLA stacks orthogonally on SRPO (kill criterion: stacking gain < 2%)\n\n3. **Baselines**: SRPO is 82.1% on LIBERO-Plus. Base VLA (SmolVLA) presumably much lower.\n\n4. **Key risks**: Transfer from synthetic MVP to real VLA flow-matching samples and K=10 covariance quality.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the key failure modes—Ledoit-Wolf regularization for covariance estimation, whether COC's self-referential signals are reliable, and whether SRPO actually provides stacking value. For LIBERO-Plus, base VLA is probably in the 30-50% range given that LIBERO-Plus is designed to expose robustness gaps, while SRPO reaches 82.1%. I need to define the critical metrics: ACR-VLA's absolute success rate improvement over base VLA and the ablation gap between CRM without conformal features versus the full system.\n\nI'm laying out three outcome scenarios—best case where per-DOF advantages transfer cleanly and K=10 covariance holds up with regularization, median case where the per-DOF benefit is smaller than expected but still works, and worst case where these claims partially fail.\n\nNow I'm working through realistic baseline numbers for LIBERO-Plus, considering that SRPO reaches 82.1% while standard LIBERO saturates at 97-99%, so the base VLA performance should be substantially lower than the SRPO-enhanced version.\n\nLet me sketch out the expected metrics across best and median scenarios—looking at the ACR-VLA improvements, ablation gaps for conformal features and per-DOF advantages, COC correlation strength, ellipsoid compression, and how much SRPO stacking could push performance higher while keeping LIBERO nominal tasks stable.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10697,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10697},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"152c9068-ec4c-424b-9b78-676ab3794382","uuid":"cc862bd6-30eb-475c-948f-7619a7c66d7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ML3J8btWbPwuZizVimo3Fz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Per-DOF advantage transfers cleanly to real VLA; all three claims validated at publishable strength\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Flow-matching VLA samples exhibit sufficient inter-sample covariance structure for CGS to exploit (not near-isotropic)\"\n      - \"K=10 with Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage yields covariance estimates accurate enough for CRM to learn meaningful per-DOF gating\"\n      - \"COC chunk overlap consistency correlates with task success strongly enough to serve as online ACI update signal\"\n      - \"Synthetic perturbation augmentation covers enough of LIBERO-Plus distribution shift for CRM to generalize\"\n      - \"SRPO-finetuned checkpoint retains exploitable epistemic uncertainty structure (not collapsed by RL fine-tuning)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      acr_vla_libero_plus_success_gain_abs: [12, 18]  # pp over base SmolVLA\n      a3_ablation_gap_no_conformal_vs_full: [8, 15]    # pp, strong Claim 1\n      a4_ablation_gap_scalar_vs_perDOF: [4, 8]         # pp\n      coc_success_spearman_rho: [0.50, 0.70]\n      aci_ellipsoid_volume_narrowing_pct: [20, 35]     # % tighter than static CP\n      srpo_stacking_gain_abs: [5, 8]                   # pp over SRPO 82.1%\n      srpo_stacked_absolute: [87, 90]\n      libero_nominal_drop: [0, 1]                      # pp degradation on in-dist\n      perturbation_dims_with_significant_gain: [5, 7]  # out of 7 LIBERO-Plus dims\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完整成立。标题级 claim: \"Inference-time dimension-selective conformal correction\n      provides orthogonal gains to training-time methods.\" 三条 claims 全部通过 kill criteria。\n      Headline: ACR-VLA 在 LIBERO-Plus 上将 base VLA 提升 X pp，叠加 SRPO 达到 ~88%+ 新 SOTA。\n      Per-DOF vs scalar ablation 提供 clean 机制验证。COC 作为自参考信号的有效性是独立贡献点。\n      可冲 CoRL oral/spotlight。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Per-DOF advantage exists but attenuated; Claim 1 survives with caveats, Claim 2 partial, Claim 3 borderline\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Flow-matching samples have covariance structure but noisier than synthetic MVP suggested; K=10 estimates are adequate but not tight\"\n      - \"Per-DOF features help CRM but advantage over scalar is modest — most gain comes from 'having any uncertainty signal' vs none\"\n      - \"COC Spearman ρ is positive but weak (0.3-0.5); ACI converges but slowly, ellipsoid narrowing modest\"\n      - \"Synthetic augmentation covers camera/noise/robot-state shifts well, but layout/language dimensions see little gain\"\n      - \"SRPO fine-tuning partially collapses uncertainty structure; stacking gain exists but is near kill threshold\"\n    number_ranges:\n      acr_vla_libero_plus_success_gain_abs: [6, 11]\n      a3_ablation_gap_no_conformal_vs_full: [3, 7]\n      a4_ablation_gap_scalar_vs_perDOF: [1, 3]         # per-DOF still > scalar but margin is thin\n      coc_success_spearman_rho: [0.30, 0.50]\n      aci_ellipsoid_volume_narrowing_pct: [10, 20]\n      srpo_stacking_gain_abs: [2, 4]\n      srpo_stacked_absolute: [84, 86]\n      libero_nominal_drop: [1, 3]\n      perturbation_dims_with_significant_gain: [3, 5]   # camera/noise/robot-state yes; layout/language no\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要调整 claims 的力度。Claim 1 从 \"per-DOF conformal features enable dimension-selective correction\"\n      软化为 \"structured uncertainty conditioning (including per-DOF features) significantly improves\n      inference-time correction, with per-DOF providing incremental gains over scalar.\" A3 gap 存在\n      但不大，故事重心从 \"per-DOF is the key\" 移向 \"any calibrated uncertainty features >> no features,\n      per-DOF is additionally beneficial.\" Claim 2 中 COC 降级为 \"promising self-referential signal\"\n      而非 \"reliable\"; 可能需要 fallback 到 episode-level ACI 作为主推方案，COC 作为 future work。\n      Claim 3 保留但措辞谨慎: \"complementary in principle, with modest empirical stacking gains.\"\n      Per-perturbation breakdown 成为重要内容——诚实展示哪些维度有效哪些无效。仍可投 CoRL poster。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Core per-DOF hypothesis does not transfer to real VLA; A3 kill criterion triggered, method reduces to generic residual policy\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Real VLA flow-matching samples are near-isotropic or have degenerate covariance; K=10 Ledoit-Wolf estimate is too noisy for CRM to extract meaningful per-DOF signal\"\n      - \"A3 ablation gap < 2%: CRM learns to correct actions but does NOT benefit from conformal features — observation-conditioned residual alone is sufficient\"\n      - \"COC Spearman ρ < 0.3 and ellipsoid narrowing < 10%: self-referential signal is unreliable, ACI provides no meaningful advantage over static calibration\"\n      - \"SRPO stacking gain < 2%: RL-finetuned policy leaves insufficient room for inference-time correction\"\n      - \"Per-DOF vs scalar gap vanishes or is negative in several perturbation dimensions\"\n    number_ranges:\n      acr_vla_libero_plus_success_gain_abs: [0, 5]\n      a3_ablation_gap_no_conformal_vs_full: [0, 2]     # kill criterion triggered\n      a4_ablation_gap_scalar_vs_perDOF: [-1, 1]        # noise-level difference\n      coc_success_spearman_rho: [0.05, 0.30]\n      aci_ellipsoid_volume_narrowing_pct: [0, 10]\n      srpo_stacking_gain_abs: [0, 2]\n      srpo_stacked_absolute: [82, 84]\n      libero_nominal_drop: [2, 5]\n      perturbation_dims_with_significant_gain: [0, 2]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 不可维持。需要重构 story 从 method paper 转为 analysis/empirical-study paper。\n      核心转向: \"When does multivariate conformal prediction help robot action correction?\n      A systematic empirical study.\" 贡献变为: (1) 负面结果的价值——证明 synthetic MVP 中的 per-DOF\n      advantage 不能 naively transfer 到 high-dimensional VLA action spaces，分析为什么\n      (covariance degeneracy, K=10 insufficient, flow-matching sample geometry); (2) 对比分析\n      CGS vs scalar CP vs DiU 在不同分布偏移类型下的行为差异，提供 practitioner guidance; (3) COC\n      信号失败模式的系统分析——什么条件下自参考校准信号可靠/不可靠。放弃 CoRL 投稿，瞄 ICLR 2027 workshop\n      或 reframe 后投 ICLR 2027 main。若 CRM 本身（不依赖 conformal features）仍有 >5% 增益，\n      可考虑退到 \"observation-conditioned residual correction\" 的 simpler story，但这与 A2C2 区分度低。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10697,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10697},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"152c9068-ec4c-424b-9b78-676ab3794382","uuid":"c7037daa-03ba-4613-baae-680df9a3741c"}
